      "text": "Momentum is built as the average of the two high-prior-return portfolios minus the average of the two low-prior-return portfolios: Mom = \u00bd(Small High + Big High) \u2212 \u00bd(Small Low + Big Low). The script reads only the first block of the file (the value-weighted monthly returns) and stops at the first non-data line after it. Months with a missing value (-99.99 or -999) are dropped.\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\nrows = []\nstarted = False\nwith open(\"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_12_2.csv\", \"r\", errors=\"ignore\") as f:\n    for line in f:\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.strip().split(\",\")]\n        ok = len(parts) >= 7 and parts[0].isdigit() and len(parts[0]) == 6\n        if ok:\n            started = True\n            rows.append(parts[:7])\n        elif started:\n            break\n\ndf = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=[\"date\", \"sl\", \"sm\", \"sh\", \"bl\", \"bm\", \"bh\"])\ndf[\"date\"] = df[\"date\"].astype(int)\nfor c in [\"sl\", \"sm\", \"sh\", \"bl\", \"bm\", \"bh\"]:\n    df[c] = pd.to_numeric(df[c], errors=\"coerce\")\n    df.loc[df[c] <= -99.99, c] = float(\"nan\")\ndf = df.dropna()\ndf[\"value\"] = 0.5 * (df[\"sh\"] + df[\"bh\"]) - 0.5 * (df[\"sl\"] + df[\"bl\"])\ndf[[\"date\", \"value\"]].to_csv(\"output.csv\", index=False)\n```",
